From a809332d874e55c01bf654eaac44bfd975d0c594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:34:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 080/114] WIP: wifi: ath11k: settle the QCA6490 v1
 configuration, drop bring-up knobs

Bake in what works on the OnePlus 9 Pro and remove the module
parameters used to find it: the part always runs as WCN6855 hw2.1,
never gets regdb.bin, and gets the WCN6855 peer, TID and MSDU counts
with the offload tables trimmed and 3 vdevs. Firmware RAM trials:

  peers/tids/msdu  vdevs  offload tables  result
  8/20/512         3      trimmed         works (old op9_small_cfg)
  16/32/1024       3      trimmed         works
  16/32/1024       4      vendor          asserts at WMI_INIT
  16/32/1056       4      vendor          asserts at WMI_INIT

The host DDR range, IOVA limit, preferred hw mode and L1SS experiments
never helped and are gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c |  4 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c  | 29 +++---------
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c  | 62 +-------------------------
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.h  |  8 +---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c  | 34 +++++---------
 5 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 115 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index be9fe5c2ad7..4f3f01996f5 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2635,8 +2635,8 @@ static int ath11k_init_hw_params(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 		ab->hw_params.regs = &wcn6855_regs;
 		ab->hw_params.fix_l1ss = false;
 		ab->hw_params.cfr_support = false;
-		/* the v1 firmware runs out of RAM on 17 vdevs; the vendor driver asks for 4 */
-		ab->hw_params.num_vdevs = 4;
+		/* the v1 firmware runs out of RAM on 17 vdevs, and on 4 */
+		ab->hw_params.num_vdevs = 3;
 		ath11k_info(ab, "QCA6490 v1: WCN6855 register map, v1 firmware limits\n");
 	}
 
